NAME
    shard - a selection's dotnet units dealt to N processes by their measured times

SYNOPSIS
    shard [--shards N] [--keep-collections] [--head REV] [--tier T] [--repo DIR] [FILE]
    shard --machine [--head REV] [--repo DIR]

DESCRIPTION
    A command of the emusen.testing module. It reads a selection (impact's
    lines, from FILE or standard input), keeps its dotnet units, and deals
    them to N shards (default 4) so a land can run N `dotnet test`
    processes at once and wait for the longest. WiseMan's Avalonia
    headless classes share one dispatcher per process, so a selection of
    49 test-minutes takes 34 wall minutes in one process; in four it
    takes about the longest shard.

    A unit's time is its seconds in the newest trial that recorded it:
    a land's TRX, or the coverage map's run (`coverage load` records
    each unit's seconds under coverage); a unit with no time counts
    20 s, and a group of cases (CLASS#KEY) with no time of its own
    counts a fortieth of its class's. The items are dealt longest first
    into the least loaded shard.

    Separate processes share no statics, but they share the machine.
    The test project's source files that show machine-wide state are
    found by a scan (a virtual pad or uinput, which every process's
    SDL sees; a listener or a literal port; a fixed path under the
    home or out/ that the file also writes; a lock on a fixed file;
    the GPU facts), and a unit is machine-global when the coverage map
    saw it execute such a file, or, for a class the map holds no rows
    for, when its own files are such; those units are dealt as one
    item and stay in one shard. FixedRunFolder is not such a file: it
    claims the next free slot (NNN.lock, FileShare.None) per process,
    which is what lets the fit audit's groups run side by side.
    --machine lists the files and the units with their reasons, from
    the sources at --head and the map. The classes of one xunit
    collection ([Collection(...)], DisableParallelization) guard state
    inside a process and are spread (decided 2026-11-02 by the tester);
    --keep-collections deals each collection as one item instead. A
    spread class that fails in a sharded land and passes alone is one
    the scan missed, and its cause goes into the scan.

    The output, tab-separated: a machine line, one line per shard, and
    a last line:

        machine  N  NOTE                    how many of the selection's
                                            units share the machine shard
        shard  N  SECONDS  UNITS  FILTER    the shard's predicted
                                            seconds, unit count and
                                            dotnet filter
        wall   SECONDS  SUM  NOTE           the longest shard, the sum,
                                            and how many units had no
                                            measured time

    land.sh runs the shards at once, each with its own log and TRX
    (dotnet-N.trx), and sums their summary lines; the backfill reads
    every dotnet*.trx of a land folder. See EmuSen_Testing.md §3.8.

EXAMPLES
    impact --base WiseMan --head pausecard | shard --shards 4 --head pausecard
    shard --keep-collections selection.txt | cut -f1-4
    shard --machine | cut -f2 | sort | uniq -c
